{
  "_readme": [
    "INTEGRATION FIXTURE. A test asset, not a seed: `data/` stays the",
    "only seed directory and `scripts/seed.ts` its only reader. The",
    "integration seed reads this directory and nothing under `data/`,",
    "on top of a `db:seed` pass that has already written the domain.",
    "",
    "This file carries `runs` rows for the example domain. The web keeps",
    "no runs module, so each row is transcribed from the stamps the web",
    "fixture modules named in its `_comment` already state: a pass",
    "opens before the document, finding or delivery it produced and",
    "closes after it, so the web's fixture path and a seeded `ar_live`",
    "tell one story. Keys beginning with an underscore are commentary,",
    "not columns.",
    "",
    "`fixtureId` is not a column. The database issues `runs.id`, and the",
    "table carries no natural key, so the member keeps an id of this",
    "file's own, which is what `llm-calls.json` names a run by.",
    "`domainSlug` names the domain by the slug `data/domains.json` seeds.",
    "",
    "`status`, `scheduledBy`, `counts` and `errors` take the shapes the",
    "workflow that closes such a pass writes: `ar-ingest` Close Run,",
    "`ar-capture` Close Capture Run and `ar-digest` Close Digest Run, each",
    "`counts` carrying every key its workflow builds. `errors` is opaque",
    "`jsonb` with no foreign key, so its `source_id` holds the source's",
    "`fixtureId` from `sources.json` and is written verbatim, never",
    "resolved; nothing may join on it. The digest's `briefings_written`",
    "counts a `briefings` row this bundle does not carry, and scoring",
    "passes are not carried at all.",
    "",
    "TIMESTAMPS ARE FIXED. `startedAt` and `finishedAt` are literal",
    "instants on or before the web's `FIXTURE_NOW` of",
    "`2026-06-11T14:30:00.000Z`, never derived from the wall clock and",
    "never left to the `started_at` column's `now()` default, so two seeds",
    "of one bundle store the same rows. No run is left `running`."
  ],
